<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rákóczi's War of Independence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1703">1703</a>–<a href="/years/1711">1711</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rákóczi's War of Independence was the Hungarian uprising of 1703–1711 against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rule, led by Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii-rakoczi">Francis II Rákóczi</a>. Rising from discontent with Habsburg absolutism, taxation and religious repression, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuruc">Kuruc</a> rebels held much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> for several years, but after defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trencin">Trencsén</a> (1708) the war ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-szatmar">Peace of Szatmár</a> (1711), which granted an amnesty while Rákóczi went into exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rakoczis-war-of-independence.jpg" alt="Rákóczi's War of Independence" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: id. Georg Philipp Rugendas · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kurucok_labancokat_hajtanak.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
